From 2436ba1f5449bccfab513e30ad27f6f6f5062d9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:52:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] assurance.machine: verify a robot cell against its declared
 safety envelope
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

WHY
  The Art. 14 register sells compliance paperwork, and so does everyone else.
  Nothing on the market takes a machine's own recorded run and checks it
  against what its manufacturer declared. That needs robotics, safety
  engineering, content addressing and regulation in one stack, which is why
  a GRC vendor cannot ship it and we can.

WHAT
  src/assurance/machine/envelope.py  declared workspace, per-mode speed limits,
                                     stop performance, sensing uncertainty —
                                     every figure carrying its own provenance
  src/assurance/machine/trace.py     what the machine did, and a Provenance that
                                     caps what the run may be used to claim
  src/assurance/machine/ssm.py       ISO/TS 15066 S = Sh+Sr+Ss+C+Zd+Zr, per term
  src/assurance/machine/limits.py    body-region limits schema and loader;
                                     this package ships no values of its own
  src/assurance/machine/verify.py    six checks, margins, and what was not checked
  src/assurance/machine/bundle.py    sealed evidence, and a re-checker for
                                     someone who does not trust the producer
  src/assurance/machine/cli.py       separation / verify / check
  src/assurance/api/machine_routes.py  the three endpoints
  examples/machine/                  a runnable cell that fails for real reasons
  deploy/assurance/MACHINE.md        how to sell it and how to run it

CUSTOMER VALUE
  An integrator carries the CE liability for a collaborative cell and today
  validates it with a tape measure and a Word document. This computes the
  protective separation distance their cell actually needs, checks a recorded
  run against it sample by sample, and seals a bundle their customer's auditor
  can re-verify without an account. The free separation calculator alone tells
  most integrators their scanner is set too close.

RISK
  Wrong numbers here are a person in hospital, so the engine is built to refuse
  rather than flatter. A check that cannot run reports unchecked, never passed.
  The tier is computed from the weakest input and cannot be passed in: a
  simulated trace never reaches validated, a datasheet stop distance caps at
  profile, an unverified limits transcription caps at community. Stopping
  distance is never extrapolated silently. No ISO values are hardcoded.

ROLLBACK
  git revert this commit. Nothing outside assurance/machine changes except an
  entitlement flag on the cell plan, one dependency in deps.py, one router in
  service.py, and a T20 per-file-ignore.

TESTS
  320 passed (75 new), ruff clean over src/assurance and the new tests.
  The shipped example is verified as part of the suite, not shipped unchecked.

SUCCESS CONDITION
  One integrator runs `machine separation` on their own cell, finds their
  scanner is set short, and pays to keep finding it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
